THOUGHT: There are escaping issues with sed. Let me use a different approach with a here document.

```bash
# Find the line number of the comment setter
line_num=$(grep -n "@comment.setter" src/cantools/database/can/signal.py | cut -d: -f1)

# Create a temporary file with the method
cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/comment_method.py
    @property
    def comment(self) -> Optional[str]:
        """The signal comment, or `None` if unavailable.

        Note that we implicitly try to return the English comment if
        multiple languages were specified.

        """
        if self.comments is None:
            return None
        elif self.comments.get(None) is not None:
            return self.comments.get(None)
        elif self.comments.get("FOR-ALL") is not None:
            return self.comments.get("FOR-ALL")

        en_comment = self.comments.get("EN")
        if en_comment is not None:
            return en_comment

        # If no preferred comment found, return the first available comment
        return next(iter(self.comments.values()), None)

EOF

# Insert the method into the file
sed -i "${line_num}r /tmp/comment_method.py" src/cantools/database/can/signal.py

# Clean up
rm /tmp/comment_method.py
```

